\par }\pard \s19\ri360\keep\widctlpar\tqc\tx4680\tqr\tx9360 {\b \tab \tab Printed }{\field{\*\fldinst {\b DATE}}{\fldrslt {\b\lang1024 07/23/97}}}
\par }\pard\plain \s1\fi1080\sb220\sa220\sl280\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar \shading1000 \b\f5\expnd-2\expndtw-10\up6\kerning28 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc394300330}Important Information{\*\bkmkend _Toc394300330}
\par \pard\plain \s2\li1080\sb140\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar \b\f5\fs22\expndtw-4\kerning28 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc394300331}The Nature of This Alpha Release{\*\bkmkend _Toc394300331}
\par \pard\plain \s15\li1080\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar \f5\fs20 3Dfxgl is a 3-D graphics library with an API which is very similar to that of OpenGL{\super {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 210 \\f "Symbol" \\s 10}{\fldrslt\f1\fs20}}}{\cs48\super \chftn 
{\footnote \pard\plain \s49\li1080\sl220\slmult0\keep\widctlpar \f4\fs18 {\cs48\super \chftn } OpenGL is a registered trademark of Silicon Graphics, Inc.}}
.  It was developed entirely by 3Dfx Interactive based on freely available information about the OpenGL state machine and interfaces.  This release is intended to give developers an early opportunity to gain experience with this API on 3Dfx Interactive ha
rdware.  It is important to keep in mind that this is an {\b ALPHA}
 release.  Not all features are supported; features supported may not offer complete functionality.  No attempt has been made to run any conformance tests.  Furthermore, please note that performa
nce optimizations are incomplete; no inferences should be drawn about the fundamental capability of 3Dfx Interactive hardware based on the behavior of applications executed with this library.
\par \pard\plain \s2\li1080\sb140\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar \b\f5\fs22\expndtw-4\kerning28 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc394300332}Unsupported Features{\*\bkmkend _Toc394300332}
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}\pard\plain \s37\fi-360\li1440\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\f5\fs20 {\b Polygon/Line Stipple}: enabling {\b GL_LINE_STIPPLE} or {\b 
GL_POLYGON_STIPPLE} will be treated as a no-op.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}{\b Texture Coordinate Generation}: {\b glTexGen}*() functions are stubbed out.  Applications depending on this functionality will most likely fail.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}{\b Texture Subimage Functions}: {\b gkTexSubImage*(), glCopyTexImage*(),} and {\b glCopyTexSubimage()} functions are stubbed out.  Applications depending on this functionality will most likely fail.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}{\b Evaluators}: {\b glEvalCoord*()} functions are stubbed out.  Applications depending on this functionality will most likely fail.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}{\b Stencil Buffer}: enabling {\b GL_STENCIL_TEST} will be treated as a no-op.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}{\b Pixel Transfer Functions}: {\b glReadPixels()} and {\b glDrawPixels()} are not implemented.  The behavior of applications depending on these functions is unpredictable.
\par {\*\bkmkstart _Toc394300333}\pard\plain \s2\li1080\sb140\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\pndec }\b\f5\fs22\expndtw-4\kerning28 Known Problems & Restrictions{\*\bkmkend _Toc394300333}
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}\pard\plain \s15\fi-360\li1440\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnb0\pni0\pnf1\pnfs20\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\f5\fs20 Under Windows{{\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 210 \\f "Symbol"
 \\s 10}{\fldrslt\f1\fs20}}}{\cs48\super \chftn {\footnote \pard\plain \s49\li1080\sl220\slmult0\keep\widctlpar \f4\fs18 {\cs48\super \chftn } Windows is a registered trademark of Microsoft Corporation}}
 95, the sample applications may fail to set the pass through mode correctly.  In general, any console application (i.e. not utilizing a Windows event loop) is susceptible to this problem.  The workaround is to manually toggle the pass through mode via CT
RL-F9.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}Textures in some programs (e.g. {\i steam}) are rendered incorrectly.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}Resizing a window so that the client area becomes zero or iconifying the window causes a DirectDraw error.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}A banner appears in the lower right hand corner of the screen when a 3Dfxgl application is running to signify that this is an Alpha release.  This banner may not be suppressed.
\par {\*\bkmkstart _Toc394300334}\pard\plain \s2\li1080\sb140\sl480\slmult1\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\pndec }\b\f5\fs22\expndtw-4\kerning28 Bugs Fixed in this release{\*\bkmkend _Toc394300334}
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}\pard\plain \fi-360\li1440\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnb0\pni0\pnf1\pnfs20\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\f4\fs20 {\f5 Texture caching does not fragment memory
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}Texture names > 512 work correctly
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}}{\b\f3 wglGetPixelDescription()}{\f5  now returns correct data
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}Line and polygon stipple implemented 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}Flashing line at the top of screen during quake fixed
\par {\*\bkmkstart _Toc394300335}}\pard\plain \s1\fi1080\sb220\sa220\sl280\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\pndec }\shading1000 \b\f5\expnd-2\expndtw-10\up6\kerning28 System Requirements{\*\bkmkend _Toc394300335}
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}\pard\plain \s15\fi-360\li1440\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\f5\fs20 Pentium{{\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 210 \\f "Symbol" \\s 10}{\fldrslt\f1\fs20}}}{
\cs48\super \chftn {\footnote \pard\plain \s49\li1080\sl220\slmult0\keep\widctlpar \f4\fs18 {\cs48\super \chftn } Pentium is a registered trademark of Intel Corporation}} Class PC or higher
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}Windows 95 or Windows NT 4.0 Operating System
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}3Dfx Interactive Voodoo Graphics-based 3D Accelerator (second monitor {\b required}) {{\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 10}{\fldrslt\f1\fs20}}}or{{\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 10}{\fldrslt
\f1\fs20}}} 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}3Dfx Interactive Voodoo Rush based 2D/3D Accelerator
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}3Dfx Interactive Glide Version 2.3 or later
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20 \'b7\tab}Microsoft OpenGL must be installed to supply needed library files.  This is the default on Windows NT, but only on some Windows 95 systems.  To verify that OpenGL is installed on a Windows 95 system, check for the e
xistence of the file named {\b\f3 \\WINDOWS\\SYSTEM\\GLU32.DLL}.  OpenGL for Windows 95 can be downloaded from the Microsoft web site from {\i\ul ftp://ftp.microsoft.com/softlib/mslfiles/oglfix.exe}
.  For further information read the Knowledge Base article Q124556.
\par \pard\plain \s1\fi1080\sb220\sa220\sl280\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar \shading1000 \b\f5\expnd-2\expndtw-10\up6\kerning28 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc394300336}Using the Driver{\*\bkmkend _Toc394300336}
\par \pard\plain \s15\li1080\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar \f5\fs20 The name of the 3Dfxgl alpha driver is {\b\f11 OpenGL32.DLL}.{\b   IMPORTANT: }this driver should {\b only}
 be copied to a user directory containing an executable to be evaluated.  Under no circumstances should this driver be copied to any system directory, including {\b  }{\b\f11 \\WINDOWS\\SYSTEM} under Windows 95 or {\b\f11 \\WINNT\\SYSTEM32}
 under Windows NT.  Similarly, do not put any directory containing {\b\f11 OpenGL32.DLL} into your path.{\b 
\par }To use this driver, copy it into the same directory as the application executable (.EXE).  For example:
\par {\b\f11 C:\\> COPY \\3dfx\\3Dfxgl\\opengl32.dll \\games\\glquake\\}{\b\f3 
\par }\pard\plain \s1\fi1080\sb220\sa220\sl280\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar \shading1000 \b\f5\expnd-2\expndtw-10\up6\kerning28 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc394300337}Creating a 3Dfxgl Application with MSVC 4.x{\*\bkmkend _Toc394300337}
\par \pard\plain \s15\li1080\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar \f5\fs20 Here is a quick, easy, step-by-step example of how to build and run a sample 3Dfxgl application with Microsoft{\super {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 210 \\f "Symbol" \\s 10}{\fldrslt
\f1\fs20}}} Visual C++ Version 4.  
\par Create a new project in Microsoft{\super {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 210 \\f "Symbol" \\s 10}{\fldrslt\f1\fs20}}} Developer Studio 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 1.\tab}\pard \s15\fi-360\li1800\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxta .}}select {\b File | New\'85 }from the main menu
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 2.\tab}select {\b Project Workspace} from the {\b New} dialog
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 3.\tab}select {\b\i Application} in {\b New Project Workspace} dialog and complete the {\b Name} and {\b Location} edit controls
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 4.\tab}click on the {\b Create} button
\par \pard \s15\li1080\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar Add the file {\b square.c} to the project.  This file is included with the alpha distribution.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 1.\tab}\pard \s15\fi-360\li1800\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxta .}}copy square.c from your 3Dfxgl installation directory into the project directory
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 2.\tab}select {\b Insert | Files into Project\'85}
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 3.\tab}select {\b square.c} from the file list
\par \pard \s15\li1080\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar Add the file opengl32.lib to the list of included library modules.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 1.\tab}\pard \s15\fi-360\li1800\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxta .}}select {\b Build | Settings}
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 2.\tab}select the {\b Link} tab in the tabbed dialog box
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 3.\tab}add {\b opengl32.lib}{\i  }to the list of files in the edit control labeled {\b Object/library modules:}
\par \pard \s15\li1080\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar Build the program.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 1.\tab}\pard \s15\fi-360\li1440\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxta .}}select {\b Build | Rebuild All}
\par \pard \s15\li1080\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar Copy over the 3Dfx driver.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 1.\tab}\pard \s15\fi-360\li1440\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxta .}}e.g. {\b\f3 C:>COPY \\install\\fxogl\\opengl32.dll \\projects\\square\\debug} 
\par \pard \s15\li1080\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar Run the program.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f5\fs20 1. \tab}\pard \s15\fi-360\li1440\sb120\sa220\sl220\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\pndec\pnb0\pni0\pnf5\pnfs20\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxta . }}select {\b Build | Debug | Go}
\par \pard\plain \s1\fi1080\sb220\sa220\sl280\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar \shading1000 \b\f5\expnd-2\expndtw-10\up6\kerning28 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc394300338}Discussion Group{\*\bkmkend _Toc394300338}
